  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef will be going to the gym for some of the next NNN days. On the iii-th day, he is free to go to the gym for AiA_iAi​ hours.\n\nChef does not want to go the gym every day, because he is lazy. But he also does not want to miss too many days without going to the gym once.\n\nThus, he decides that he will go **every alternate day**. He may go on days 1,3,5,…1, 3, 5, \\ldots1,3,5,… or days 2,4,6,…2, 4, 6, \\ldots2,4,6,….\n\nFind the maximum total hours he can invest in the gym.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line contains NNN - the number of days.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​, the number of hours he is free for on the iii-th day.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the maximum total hours he can invest.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N≤1001 \\le N \\le 1001≤N≤100",
      "1≤Ai≤1001 \\le A_i \\le 1001≤Ai​≤100"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n3\n2 5 4\n4\n6 2 1 7\n1\n5",
        "output": "6\n9\n5",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : Chef can train on days 1,31, 31,3 to spend a total of 666 hours at the gym. On the other hand, day 222 alone would only be 555 hours."
      }
    ]
  },
